d mechanism effects: the 6.950 million June level supplies the persistence anchor; positive multi-year growth adds 0.05 million; weak technology hiring subtracts 0.02 million; no identified July-specific policy or classification change warrants another adjustment."},{"kind":"math","text":"Prior/update/interval: persistence model prior = June 2026's 6.950 million; historical sample = 2021-2025 annual averages of 5.688, 6.171, 6.502, 6.386, and 6.711 million; successive changes are +0.483, +0.331, -0.116, and +0.325 million, giving sigma = 0.236 million. Adjustments are +0.050 million for longer-run momentum and -0.020 million for soft hiring, yielding 6.950 + 0.050 - 0.020 = 6.980 million. The normal 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 1.28*0.236 = 0.302 million, implying 6.678 to 7.282 million, rounded to 6.68 to 7.28 million."},{"kind":"text","text":"Upside risk comes from faster AI-related hiring, labor-force re-entry, or favorable CPS sampling and would land above the interval if employment exceeds 7.28 million. Downside risk comes from layoffs, weak hiring, or adverse sampling and would land below the interval if employment is under 6.68 million; either outcome would be outside the interval."},{"kind":"forecast","point":6.98,"ciLow":6.68,"ciHigh":7.28}]}
