 the latest NSA CPS occupation level with a negative July seasonal update. The January-June sequence is choppy but centered near 7.8 million, while July 2025 fell 0.276 million from June and remained 0.227 million below July 2024."},{"kind":"math","text":"Prior/update/interval: persistence prior = June 2026 first print of 7.759 million; historical sample = January-June 2026 first prints [7.905, 7.742, 7.685, 7.883, 7.912, 7.759]. Successive changes are [-0.163, -0.057, +0.198, +0.029, -0.153] million, whose sample standard deviation is sigma = 0.149 million. Apply a -0.200 million update for July seasonality and weak year-over-year level momentum, with no separate policy adjustment: 7.759 - 0.200 = 7.559. The normal 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 1.28*0.149 = 0.191 million, implying bounds 7.559 +/- 0.191 = [7.368, 7.750]."},{"kind":"text","text":"Upside risk is an abrupt rebound like April 2026, which could put the print above 7.750 million. Downside risk is a July seasonal drop materially larger than 2025's 0.276 million or renewed manufacturing weakness; a decline exceeding 0.391 million from June would land below the interval. Either outcome would be outside the interval."},{"kind":"forecast","point":7.559,"ciLow":7.368,"ciHigh":7.75}]}
./records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-21/2026-07-21t01-11-54z-bls-cps-employed-people-by-occupation-production-2026-07/revision_prompt.md:135:{"summary":"Draft is mostly publishable, but it should tighten resolver wording to the canonical Table A-19 target and better support the large July seasonal adjustment with a broader or explicitly limited seasonal sample.","requiredFixes":[{"rubricItem":"resolver","severity":"warning","summary":"The resolver/source text says Table A-13/A-19 even though the ledger binding is cpseea19.htm, CPS Employment Situation Table A-19, field Production occupations; the official release date also appears to be 2026-08-07 while the ledger resolutionDate is 2026-08-06.","actionRequested":"State the resolver as canonical Table A-19/cpseea19.htm and first-print July 2026 value, keep resolutionDate tied to the registered 2026-08-06 ledger date, and keep the official-calendar discrepancy as an explicit note rather than blending A-13/A-19 in the resolver."},{"rubricItem":"update","severity":"warning","summary":"The -0.200 million movement from June persistence is material and is mainly justified by one June-to-July comparison from 2025 plus a qualitative weak-momentum claim.","actionRequested":"Either add a short multi-year June-to-July NSA production-occupation seasonal sample, or explicitly say the update is mostly a judgmental shrinkage from the single 2025 seasonal drop and recent soft year-over-year context."}],"optionalSuggestions":["Include the June 2025 value in historicalContext if it remains central to the seasonal update.","Clarify that archived A-13 references are evidence lookups only if older releases used different table numbering, while the target resolver remains Table A-19."]}
